[{"id":"VRCE-1-29-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":1,"english":"Then those princes, repressors of foes, cognizant of place, and time, and words, thus spoke to Kuśika's son agreeably to time and place, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f68933135c41bc961373a85557e86874c9ea02e7309eb7ae4d17906f7d9838c","compact":"cd5824a2b81aa35585f79a0907c6f654b17c6ba20531e56d982065c32ce33dbe","nasal":"cd5824a2b81aa35585f79a0907c6f654b17c6ba20531e56d982065c32ce33dbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":2,"english":"O adorable one, do you tell us as to the time when we should oppose those rangers of the night! Let not that hour pass away!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b826c6e0ec2252d8cb8904723333119f2f38fd8eec615759d742906e0a94f27","compact":"35545cce9f48e79ec128f1b7bb730dbefaf475a6d3e185903e780f8c3ab3e9b0","nasal":"22a9b3c411b4caf4f323be9541296642fa21cda3589656e567ac92823310a428"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":3,"english":"Upon the two Kākutsthas' saying this, and finding them prompt for the encounter, those ascetics well-pleased, fell to extolling the sons of the king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1fa33ed5564d6c0e55c5b0824d073871a2eaae0328c54cf7dfcbcc09ca51d8f1","compact":"529365cac63d2efb9fe1a1aea0b7cfb424f1cbc6473400abebf73177fe44c1aa","nasal":"529365cac63d2efb9fe1a1aea0b7cfb424f1cbc6473400abebf73177fe44c1aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":4,"english":"For six nights from to-day, you should protects us. This ascetic has been initiated into the sacrifice, and must, therefore, observe taciturnity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad6ec13a5e97239efcbe083be19bed2d3a7997abe46204c697ab1a76ab29592d","compact":"cf5adc560705da3b35c3f1022b0437d3b7c0a7fcce2df63794139e7f76730f21","nasal":"cf5adc560705da3b35c3f1022b0437d3b7c0a7fcce2df63794139e7f76730f21"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":5,"english":"Hearing these words of theirs, those illustrious princes, renouncing sleep, began to guard the hermitage day and night; and those heroic and mighty archers protected that best of ascetics and subduer of enemies.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9b64f64fa29214aa9ede4c9891c1e90372dcdb976fbec770bfb405b68154e12","compact":"2dc5d16747aeee8f9b974f602e591da8e4dcc6c081657a5f7a444391d0b8b5fe","nasal":"2dc5d16747aeee8f9b974f602e591da8e4dcc6c081657a5f7a444391d0b8b5fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":6,"english":"Hearing these words of theirs, those illustrious princes, renouncing sleep, began to guard the hermitage day and night; and those heroic and mighty archers protected that best of ascetics and subduer of enemies.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be5abd214c513f0c42ec6c83971b9d8159016ac9b03d985a2754b6402919dba7","compact":"074bf385000d8c9df8103e31498530c0d3c4266574532f4b51fb0bbc83a2c045","nasal":"074bf385000d8c9df8103e31498530c0d3c4266574532f4b51fb0bbc83a2c045"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":7,"english":"When time had thus gone by and the sixth day had arrived, Rāma said to Sumitrā's son. Being well equipped, be you vigilant!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d760daa5635b29fefce5e44995dabb4233749cfc1e01b1b157d13c816c2d9ab9","compact":"16c6e2d7605c15bafeb66b1e105d36f810dfe94a3663814397bdf87f26450766","nasal":"16c6e2d7605c15bafeb66b1e105d36f810dfe94a3663814397bdf87f26450766"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":8,"english":"When Räma, manifesting emotion, and being eager for encounter, had said this, the priests and spiritual guides lit up the altar. And along with Viśvāmitra and the family priests, they lit up the altar furnished with Kusa, and Kasa, and ladles, and faggots, and flowers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e1838b514735b2b416c96b5cc9367e59a643ae0ecf4f8b76d9d563641d9c3f07","compact":"16100176f21511040292ccc443e6ea5bdec0f1268f76ab01fada25e9294945b7","nasal":"16100176f21511040292ccc443e6ea5bdec0f1268f76ab01fada25e9294945b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":9,"english":"And as reciting mantras, they were about to duly engage in that sacrifice, there arose a mighty and dreadful uproar in the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c773b76af9988479d0adcf7679479082ef90f8587849229c8147d93b66e036ed","compact":"83cbbbc07bbe2c42f789a86c931ae3156c4637ceec0d83f99b5f08ec28fb5042","nasal":"a118953b3cf043f4ce2bb2458caca615a2d75f4c68cfad28cd34aaf331d18198"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":10,"english":"And as in the rains, masses of clouds appear enveloping the firmament, the Rākşasas, displaying illusions in that wise, began to rush onward. And Mārīca and Subāhu together with their followers coming in dreadful forms, began to shower down blood upon the altar.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"698af8414dddf161bebc678a3c3905130774cad6b77729406967127191c416d6","compact":"97c62c53667329a96bc2c8ba6d95cdf3934492ac0734eee9f9851ceedbd997af","nasal":"97c62c53667329a96bc2c8ba6d95cdf3934492ac0734eee9f9851ceedbd997af"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":11,"english":"And as in the rains, masses of clouds appear enveloping the firmament, the Rākşasas, displaying illusions in that wise, began to rush onward. And Mārīca and Subāhu together with their followers coming in dreadful forms, began to shower down blood upon the altar.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f36b3f79192877072ac3d0ae19b4b8578edd99923ca4f7a96be2e827de7003de","compact":"8da39e20282557dfae0c1f99c1352f4bddfea5d7096b354255f7ae650e57269b","nasal":"8da39e20282557dfae0c1f99c1352f4bddfea5d7096b354255f7ae650e57269b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":12,"english":"And on seeing the altar deluged with gore, Rāma suddenly rushed forward, and behold them in the sky. And suddenly seeing them rushing in amain, the lotus-eyed Rāma fixing his gaze at Laksmana, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8b5442707e8c1868055969a85f023efa31d6e6cf23ad373459bfc8039095bfc","compact":"4fcdbd93649e53a451ea5d5206f0947944a03ed26074f357fa56e1dd70f71906","nasal":"07b65832fc48cbb779b62b021129e2ad382457a93ad6bc4ff8d8bff915b69c71"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":13,"english":"Behold O Lakşmana, by means of a Mānava weapon, I shall, without doubt, drive away the wicked; flesh-eating Raksasas, even as the wind drive away clouds before it. Surely I cannot bring myself to slay such as these.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c43c29522389bb1b3ba4758fc818389c98a216ce19fb698d0949d6fc417d0abd","compact":"dd62521fef9154c2a10626c17bf79401ff810d8167919060b2554dff1b7d27c0","nasal":"dd62521fef9154c2a10626c17bf79401ff810d8167919060b2554dff1b7d27c0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":14,"english":"Saying this, that descendant of Raghu, Rāma, in vehemence fixing on his bow an exceedingly mighty and gloriously-dazzling Mānava weapon, discharged it in great wrath at Mārīca's chest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"890da451ab04f10d528aec1cf95776482b087f20af192456893cc79e6b9e7bc3","compact":"07b912547388695fc9fcb9a82caac57878ddb20a77144b61fefa9c5ce6a1c9ea","nasal":"07b912547388695fc9fcb9a82caac57878ddb20a77144b61fefa9c5ce6a1c9ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":15,"english":"And wounded by that foremost of Mānava weapons, Mārīca carried off a sheer hundred Yojanas, dropped in the midst of the ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.564,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"474edc89cee6358e15456ef28aa36a6be9abbd2bf053a831e58469c09e4c181b","compact":"4ad3795366de4a6df5e73436e683c80bec8c37120a7749836af92cadea03215c","nasal":"4ad3795366de4a6df5e73436e683c80bec8c37120a7749836af92cadea03215c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":16,"english":"And finding Mārica senseless, and whirling, and afflicted by the might of the weapon, and overcome, Rama addressed Laksmana, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa3c94ab58735bd888888b261c8f210e154ed82716d82ce8bd3e8bba45c3c075","compact":"28572b243df39c09a6790a281ee4a3fa29c0fa92cb59100a16a7fffa9103fd82","nasal":"966b1572c710254a92a5e586effbbb5c8c04939f524932a293a2062f5486e4da"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":17,"english":"Behold, O Laksmana, this Manava weapon first used by Manu, depriving him of his senses has carried him off, and yet has not taken his life!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.73,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c116e0bf33e756bf47a1fb419a2fb3fbfd2c9a76f436a070a1c3620841ade9d","compact":"e3f704b6ad01fb29d73f4e5be0fabaa03cce4958a2b209a297836cd451aa3de0","nasal":"525d66952ffe760b40c8a6e847c1f3de7efa09ced97656ef7c7b1d330168a263"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":18,"english":"But these shameless, wicked, and blooddrinking Raksasas, delighting in wrong-doing, these disturbers of sacrifices, will I slaughter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3579927b423c55353d87eca5cee788da529273d964981584f60813d27414a469","compact":"391c141aaf68243e0fc435b54e75b2045e55f0d98916b4780629278f667ced10","nasal":"1df27dfdb2c18cd8b51f882fef50ee41745ffda3b5813fc21ed9c9ebed3d82e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":19,"english":"Having said this, anon showing to Lakşmaņa his lightness of hand, Raghu's descendant took out a mighty Āgneya weapon, and discharged it at the breast of Subāhu. Thereat being pierced with that shaft, he fell down upon the ground. Then taking a Vāyavya weapon, the illustrious and exceedingly generous Rāghava, bringing delight to those ascetics, slew the rest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61168a4c6969f2fad450375f6da759850c8f11657992d1cb4671ea22d70accd7","compact":"425dfbf2b3c870cf05883d50b724e8de8f9ebec55861d696dcb60dc755c8fa6a","nasal":"f319e6e25b0314b0ae0d69636c579c9103d91149af83c7ba9a5670fe6d513dfa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":20,"english":"Having said this, anon showing to Lakşmaņa his lightness of hand, Raghu's descendant took out a mighty Āgneya weapon, and discharged it at the breast of Subāhu. Thereat being pierced with that shaft, he fell down upon the ground. Then taking a Vāyavya weapon, the illustrious and exceedingly generous Rāghava, bringing delight to those ascetics, slew the rest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"520ab006adcf1ff7b54c349e4e815d9679f6cdaee2e6aa3505cd8b954f99a58f","compact":"5317f802017e4a186ac3af183b3ebf6f7141420c4c06eca801769e82ddff73a5","nasal":"5317f802017e4a186ac3af183b3ebf6f7141420c4c06eca801769e82ddff73a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":21,"english":"Having destroyed all those Rākşasas disturbing sacrifices, Raghu's descendant was honoured by the saints, even as Indra in day of yore, after having vanquished the Asuras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04449b96f5a9f9feae7dbf16b5c3930cdf4ea3ef41b0e105f678a11f90e4c323","compact":"7d4e09b4ae0870cb5516bcc2ae3f2fcf812a3d0ab8875c9fb2c246bbb454537d","nasal":"5cffba5c0d1881e6eb2c0ef9349b32c62c33362cfa2ece8bb0ea7a1ba0c766aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":22,"english":"When the sacrifice had been completed, the mighty ascetic Viśvāmitra, beholding all sides cleared of Rākṣasas, spoke to Käkutstha, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"44a2fdf531e6b3dc6210143c2a8f29d8a67766fa59c0d7dbc5f415e7ded50d08","compact":"c32e71414f44bb3de7fb9e8fa10a066201025c29cdb734872cd6fae23fbd9a0a","nasal":"c32e71414f44bb3de7fb9e8fa10a066201025c29cdb734872cd6fae23fbd9a0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-29-23","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":29,"verse":23,"english":"O mighty-armed one, I have obtained my desire; and you have executed your preceptor's mandate. And, O illustrious hero, you have truly made this a Siddhāśrama. Having thus extolled Rāma, he took Rāma and Lakşmaņa, to perform his evening devotions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-30-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1029023","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba5e80b70301082a8e912bf955771f05aa8e218c5eb70b426c3f6f471132ec09","compact":"283a462cd2f22b4fb6be30569d9ecd9b9da300c319c0b29d4a262f83a5ffa589","nasal":"283a462cd2f22b4fb6be30569d9ecd9b9da300c319c0b29d4a262f83a5ffa589"}}]
